{
  "title": "RTC Media Quality \u2014 Norrsken Kigali",
  "uid": "norrsken-rtc-001",
  "tags": [
    "norrsken",
    "rtc",
    "voice",
    "video",
    "sla"
  ],
  "timezone": "Africa/Kigali",
  "refresh": "120s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-3h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "About This Dashboard",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Tracks FortiGate SD-WAN kernel SLA metrics (latency, jitter, packet loss) for appids explicitly classified by FortiGuard as **RTC-VOICE / RTC-VIDEO** \u2014 real-time media traffic only, excluding signaling, chat, and file-transfer traffic from the same platforms.\n\n**IMPORTANT \u2014 confirmed data availability per platform (checked 2026-08-26):**\n\n| Platform | SD-WAN kernel data available? |\n|---|---|\n| Google Meet (48983) | YES |\n| Zoom Meeting (47385) | YES |\n| Signal (43847) | YES |\n| Webex (16350) | YES |\n| FaceTime (24426) | YES (very sparse) |\n| Microsoft Teams Audio (54418) | **NO** |\n| Microsoft Teams Video (54419) | **NO** |\n| WhatsApp VoIP (40698) | **NO** |\n\nTeams and WhatsApp calls generate substantial real traffic but FortiGate's SD-WAN kernel engine never produces a performance measurement for them on this configuration \u2014 likely because this traffic isn't currently matched by a firewall/SD-WAN rule that triggers kernel health-check evaluation. This is a FortiGate configuration limitation, not a gap in this dashboard's queries. Panels for Teams/WhatsApp will show 'No data' \u2014 this reflects reality, not a broken query.\n\n**Data source:** `rtc_media_bridge.py` \u2014 polls Elasticsearch every 120s, aggregates the last 120s of SD-WAN SLA log entries per app+interface using real `stats` aggregations (avg/max) for latency and jitter (confirmed numeric fields). Packet loss, reply jitter, origin jitter, and server response time are keyword-mapped in this ES index and use latest-value only, not a true window average."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Active RTC Sessions Right Now",
      "description": "Shows sample_count per app for the current window \u2014 a nonzero value means FortiGate logged at least one real-time media SLA measurement for that app recently, i.e. a call is likely in progress. SOURCE: fortigate_rtc_sla_sample_count, label app. Zero or missing = no active call detected for that platform.",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "gray",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "NO CALL",
                  "color": "gray"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
          },
          "expr": "fortigate_rtc_sla_sample_count{site=\"norrsken-kigali\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "RTC Latency \u2014 Average & Peak",
      "description": "Per-app latency for real-time media traffic only (RTC-VOICE/RTC-VIDEO appids). SOURCE: fortigate_rtc_sla_latency (avg) and fortigate_rtc_sla_latency_max (peak within each 120s aggregation window), label app. Derived from Elasticsearch field fortinet.firewall.latency (confirmed float type) via a real stats aggregation across every SD-WAN SLA log entry in the window, not just the latest single reading. Thresholds: Green <80ms, Yellow 80-150ms, Red >150ms.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "decimals": 1,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 80
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 150
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max",
            "last"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
          },
          "expr": "fortigate_rtc_sla_latency{site=\"norrsken-kigali\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}} \u2014 avg",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
          },
          "expr": "fortigate_rtc_sla_latency_max{site=\"norrsken-kigali\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}} \u2014 max",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
